{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1551784-blood-junkies-brutal-d100-vampire-roleplay-pay-what-you-want","id":1551784,"title":"Blood Junkies, brutal d100 vampire roleplay. Pay what you want.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-20T07:43:02-07:00","id":1551784,"title":"Blood Junkies, brutal d100 vampire roleplay. Pay what you want.","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/519933/blood-junkies\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/prod.../blood-junkies</a><br /> <br /> This started as a Mythras hack for VtM and grew into its own thing. Available in print and pdf. If you want a fast game that gives you an experience like Near Dark, this is it.<br /> <br /> Brutal Vampires<br /> Vampire roleplay has never been so straightforward with fast and simple percentile mechanics, character driven roleplay and a clear morality system based around death.<br /> <br /> Personal Horror<br /> No ancient blood gods, end time scenarios, or iron-clad hierarchy, the horror in this game is about you and your Humanity. Detailed psychology helps guide your roleplay.<br /> <br /> Cinematic play<br /> One percentile roll tells you success and damage. No combat rounds or initiative, fights happen in real time. Designed for fast resolution that lets you stay in character<img title=\"Screenshot_19.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1889_1750430384221_35\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1889\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1889\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1889&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Screenshot_19.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> Some of the biggest differences between this and vtm:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Every time you drink blood you roll to see if you kill the victim. This changes the vibe a lot, murder is now a common occurence and you have to get good at covering it up.</li> <li>There's no big vampire society, there's not that many vampires in the world.</li> <li>Level 1 Powers are more powerful.</li> <li>Humanity is more clear. No hierarchy of sins, no paths, it's about murder and seeing people as individuals. Gaining Humanity is now easier to do and a viable arc.</li> <li>The consequences for Anathema (diablerie) are about gang wars, not prince law.</li> <li>New Powers (disciplines)</li> <li>No Clans, your primary Power determines your Curse. (insanity, monstrous, no reflection, etc)</li> <li>Percentile resolution means fast. Improvement by doing keeps roleplay front and center.</li> <li>No political axe to grind, I keep my views out of the game.</li> <li>Lore is kept to a minimum and rules are kept brief. The focus is on the player characters and their personal journeys, not a metaplot with famous NPCs.</li> </ol>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28839-space_roadie","name":"Space_Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28839_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}